  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "1wv/lG5x/SHtGG8tZl01H35vtyY=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:30:22.708Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "Creetion focuses on three platforms \u2014 SAP, OutSystems and Flowable \u2014 and that narrowness is the finding: it is the deepest Flowable commitment recorded anywhere in the directory sweep. Most firms in the same cohort list Flowable among a dozen or more alliances, where a single platform is a line item rather than a bet.\n\nDepth of commitment is a better predictor of carrier behaviour than certification tier. A firm with three platforms has staked its positioning on them, so the Flowable practice has real consultants attached and a pipeline that depends on process orchestration selling well. That is precisely the seam the record-layer argument attaches to, and it makes Creetion a partner with something to gain from strengthening the Flowable story rather than a partner with one more logo to place.\n\nThe complication in the same record is OutSystems, one of the other two platforms \u2014 an app-layer position of the kind the screen treats as slot occupancy elsewhere. So the Flowable strength and a potential conflict sit in the same three-platform list, which is worth resolving before a pitch. The row is ranked priority 2 and its provenance is the Flowable Partner Finder mined on 2026-08-18; it has not been imprint-swept, so contact and legal details are still unverified.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**2 \u00b7 next**\n- Creetion (NL Breda) \u2014 creetion.com\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> Flowable is one of only three platforms they focus on (SAP, OutSystems, Flowable) \u2014 deepest Flowable commitment in the directory \u00b7 SOURCE: Flowable Partner Finder (flowable.com/company/partners), mined 2026-08-18. NOT imprint-swept.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:30:22.708191Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:30:22.708195Z"
    }
  },
